                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_08\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes KVMPhysicalDisk.java line \"rbdOpts += \"\\\\\\\\:\" + monPort;\" to \"rbdOpts += \"\\\\:\" + monPort;\" (i.e. a Java source string that produces two literal backslashes before the colon is reduced to one), fixing a \"double-escape\" of the rados monitor port separator, as described in the commit message (\"Fix double-escape issue while creating rbd disk options ... the rados host/monitor port was double escaped\").\n\nTracing the history of this exact code across the candidates, the method KVMPhysicalDisk.RBDStringBuilder(...) is first introduced in candidate_08, which adds:\n\n    rbdOpts = \"rbd:\" + image;\n    rbdOpts += \":mon_host=\" + monHost + \"\\\\\\\\:\" + monPort;\n\nThis is the very first appearance of the \"\\\\\\\\:\" (double-escaped backslash) pattern in the codebase \u2014 no prior candidate (01-07) contains any reference to RBDStringBuilder, mon_host, or monPort. Subsequent candidates (11, 12, 13, 14, 16, 19) only restructure surrounding logic (e.g., splitting the port-append into a conditional, reformatting call sites, adding rbd_default_format/client_mount_timeout options) but all preserve the same buggy \"\\\\\\\\:\" double-escaped separator introduced in candidate_08. Candidate_20 is the actual bug fix itself (its diff is byte-for-byte identical to fix_commit_diff.txt, changing \"\\\\\\\\:\" to \"\\\\:\"), confirming that the double backslash had persisted unchanged from its origin in candidate_08 all the way to the fix.\n\nSince candidate_08 is the commit that first wrote the double-escaped \"\\\\\\\\:\" string that every later commit (until the fix) merely inherited, it is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
